From 5cb56ad16f191e936f9a023574bf005888b9a751 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: arena-ai-coding-agent <arena-ai-coding-agent@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 29 Aug 2026 06:47:33 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Fix subagent model inheritance after disabling official
 DeepSeek adapter

The patch removes the official DeepSeek adapter from the active base
composition, but agents and in-process subagents were still resolving the
removed deepseek-official route as their default. Subagent children only
inherited the creation-time parent options, so they failed with 'no
adapter registered for provider deepseek-official' even when the parent
session was using an available provider.

- Repoint agent-default-model from the removed deepseek-official route to
  the pi-ai deepseek route for the same model family.
- Resolve child provider/model/maxTokens from the parent session's latest
  request header (the live route actually used) before falling back to
  creation-time options.
---
 README.md                             |  2 +-
 docs/index.html                       |  4 +-
 patches/open-authority-web-only.patch | 59 +++++++++++++++++++++++++--
 3 files changed, 59 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

